WEBVTT

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:08.190
Don't touch it, don't touch it
sawaranaide sawaranaide yawarakana ai de

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:11.740
Watch over it softly, with sweet love
funwari to mimamottete ne

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.280
All right, all right, okay, okay?
oorai oorai OK OK?

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:32.590
Even though the third try went bad
sandome no shoujiki ga bacchiri shippai shitemo

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:38.100
the Earth is still turning, round and round!
soredemo chikyuu wa mawatteru guru guru!

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:43.810
I'm honest to my desire and innocently greedy
yokubou ni shoujiki de mujaki ni donyoku desu

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:48.900
You just realized that? How slow...
imagoro kizuita no? osoi yo nee

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:55.950
Please give me all the goodies that reflect in my eyes
kono me ni utsuru suteki wo zeenbu kudasai

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:01.200
Being able to say what you like is a blessing
sukina mono wo suki to ieru shi-a-wa-se

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:07.000
Don't drop it, don't drop it, scoop it with both hands
otosanaide otosanaide ryoute de sukutte

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.420
Surround it with a lot of love
ookime no ai de tsutsunde

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.090
Thank you, thank you, berry much
sankyuu sankyuu berry macchi

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:19.970
Round, sour, gentle, absent-minded girls...
maarukutte suppakutte fuwari bonyari onna no ko

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:25.440
If we make a pinky-promise I'll never let go
yubikiri shichatta nara hanarenaizo

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.350
Strawberry, berry, berry
ichigo berry berry

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.360
I cried, furry furry
naita furry furry

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.240
That's impossible, impossible
sore wa murry murry

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.110
Ah, give me a break - berry berry!
akkan bee berry berry!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.960
Oh well...

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:36.090
Everyday.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.050
I'm home!

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.970
I feel lazy.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:45.010
Aren't you just drunk? Go back to your own room.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.810
It's going to be a long holiday, starting from tomorrow, eh?

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.690
Do we have any plans?

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.230
Not really.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.530
How come we don't have any plans?

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.360
Don't you think it's deplorable to be trapped at home despite the long holiday?

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.280
To you, it's the same as usual anyway.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.240
Besides, it's pointless to complain to me.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.660
"Long holidays aren't related to me anyway," eh?

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.500
I see, you're so cool.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.130
Hey, I too want to go out during the long holiday.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.510
Oh, you finally spilled it.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:20.550
Want to drink some?

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.600
My classmate said that her family would be going to Hawaii.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.510
How nice...

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.730
"How nice," eh? Do you want to go to Hawaii?

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.440
Hawaii is a world of ice on the other side of the Earth.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.190
Don't lie. I know about Hawaii.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.400
Don't be so serious. You can't go anyway.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.110
For the long holiday...

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.280
We plan to stay at home.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.950
Really? I thought you would go out or something.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.160
You went to Britain recently, didn't you?

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.500
Ah? Yes.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.750
My cousins showed me around London and some other places...

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.090
How nice.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:01.220
We couldn't even understand each other. I was worn out.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:02.180
Eh?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.930
Those British kids...

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.890
Next time I will leave them alone in Sugamo's Togenuki Jizou Avenue

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.770
and let them get totally lost in there.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.640
I won't be satisfied until I pay them back ten times for what I got...

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.060
Ana-chan, did something happen?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.990
M-Matsuri-chan, what are you planning to do for the long holidays?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:25.410
Erm, I'm going to my grandfather's place for the coming summer holiday.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.820
Summer holiday?

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.870
Spring just began though.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:33.500
Yeah, that's why I have to start storing up my physical strength now,

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.500
so I can't go out during the long holidays.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.290
What kind of physical strength is that?

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.760
It's just like animal's hibernation.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.550
It's Matsuri-chan, so I will just let it slip.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.010
I-I see.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:48.470
Ah... Anywhere is fine, I just want to go out.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.430
Why are you being sulky? You're not a kid...

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:52.060
What the heck are you doing?

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.140
Onee-chan, you were the one who brought it up first.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.110
Cheer up, Chi-chan.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:06.200
I have no plans or any pocket money either, but I'm living industriously.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.030
Th-Thank you.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.450
Have some of these.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.990
Here.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.170
What? You don't want any?

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:22.090
Hey, I made that cake, didn't I?

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.380
Geez, how long do you plan to sulk?

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.840
Nah, it's because you're fanning the flames.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.350
I will take that out then.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.140
What's "that"?

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.010
Eh?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.940
I'm sure it's around here...

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:38.900
Found it!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.150
Yeah, right.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:44.820
Kokumin Shukusha Izu-style lodging coupon.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.450
Onee-chan, what is this about?

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.530
Erm, let's see...

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.700
I got it in a lottery at the supermarket on New Year's Day.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.500
I forgot about it because I wasn't interested.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.000
What is a Kokumin Shukusha?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.880
A cheap facility that can be used by health insurance policy holders...

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.380
Ah, you mean a youth hostel?

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.340
You could say that.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:11.890
Hey, let's go.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:12.640
I don't want to.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:13.970
It's too tiresome.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:19.270
What's that? You made me all excited about it. Nobu-nee, you stupid fool.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:23.650
Poor Chika-san, always has nothing planned for her.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.030
Yeah. If it were me, I would cry.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.990
You're being pitied, Chi.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:32.950
Ah, no... That's not what I meant...

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:36.330
But if just me and Chi go, it will be boring.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.410
Yes, I'll join you guys!

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:39.620
You're rejected.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.250
Nobu-nee, you stupid fool!
Nobu-nee, you stupid fool!

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.050
Oh, you two are in harmony.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:44.880
I don't care.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:45.670
You flat-chested...

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.260
She got you, eh, Chi?

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.260
Erm, Onee-sama...

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.640
I want to go too, if you don't mind.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.770
Right?

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:58.850
Eh?

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.980
Matsuri-chan has just built up enough physical strength, too.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:05.400
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.740
What? Does everyone want to go?

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.070
I guess it can't be helped. If that's the case, let's go.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.370
Oh, really?

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.120
But it's not like it's a novel place or anything.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.160
Don't complain when you get there.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.370
Okay. Yay! We're going out!

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:21.960
What kind of place is Izu?
Okay. Yay! We're going out!

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.250
What kind of place is Izu?

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.630
Let's see. Izu is...

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.590
A suspension bridge. I saw it before on pictures.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:31.720
That's right. There are alligators that like bananas who live underneath the bridge

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.220
and protect the lighthouse.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.810
Speaking of Izu, the dancers there are famous.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.390
Dancers?

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:02.870
<i>Because of a sudden news report,
broadcasting of the movie will be postponed indefinitely.</i>

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:03.870
Eh?

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.080
<i>Talking about Izu, Izu's...</i>

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:14.590
My... dancers...

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.600
<i>Hamamatsu area, precipitation percentage is 20 percent.</i>

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:28.440
<i>Next is Izu district. It will be cloudy from midnight to early morning.</i>

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.610
<i>The weather will be fine during the day, so you don't need to worry about bringing an umbrella.</i>

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.700
<i>It will be a perfect weather for going out.</i>

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.070
<i>Well then, next is...</i>

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:58.510
Aren't you glad that the weather is nice?

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.100
I wonder if it's because of teruterubouzu.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.640
I'm sure it is, since we made them together.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.400
Right, Onee-chan?

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.690
Possibly.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.400
Well then, let's go.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.200
Miu, please guide the car out of the road.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:14.860
Okay.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.780
Departure, all right!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.580
Okay, do a tail slide right there!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.540
Spin for two and a half circles!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.750
Guys, did you bring everything?

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.290
Yes.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.250
Okay then, let's go!

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.920
I'm looking forward to it.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:36.380
Yeah, we're going out. Yahoo!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:36.760
Yahoo!

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:37.890
Hey, wait!
Yahoo!

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.600
Hey, wait! You forgot something!

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:00.570
Ah, refreshing scenery.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:04.540
And refreshing music.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.870
This is the best.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.670
Excuse me...

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.210
Do you have any other CDs?

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:15.050
Why? Talking about driving, this is the kind of music that you listen to.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.470
Geez.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:18.340
Ah, what?

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.510
About how much further till we get to Izu?

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:23.930
Ah, about 20 kilometers.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:24.930
Probably...

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.850
We will be there soon.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:27.810
Y-Yeah.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:31.650
Let's play some songs to liven things up.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.270
Do you have any requests?

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.570
Mori no Kuma-san.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.110
Eh?

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.570
Mori no Ishimatsu will be nice too.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.780
Nah, I don't have that kind of CD.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.700
Ah, how about the one you bought the other day?

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:45.490
Remember? The one with the beautiful-sounding guitar...

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:49.960
Eight hours later

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.920
Hey, we're here.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:04.180
Th-The smoke after taking a spin feels special.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.520
Eh? You were in there?

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.520
You should have said something, if you knew it was going to take eight hours.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.990
Shut up. If I didn't get lost, it would have only taken two hours.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:19.950
So you did get lost after all!

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.660
It couldn't be helped. There's no GPS system installed in this car.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.120
Anyway, where's the toilet?

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.710
How pretty...

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:43.050
Let's see... The address, eh...

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:47.260
Isn't this fruit the same as the one we saw in the illustrated book of plants?

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:50.940
Yeah. It's way prettier than the picture.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:53.060
Thanks for waiting. Let's go to the room.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:54.860
Okay.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:05.070
Chi, hand me the newspapers from over there.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.080
Huh?

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.200
Good afternoon.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.620
Ah. Did you make it?

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.080
It leaked a bit.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:15.250
Don't get it into the laundry of our place.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.040
Okay.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:27.260
Meow. I'm the always cheerful cat, meow.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:31.230
What is with this mood? Isn't it exactly the same as our usual room?

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.770
That's what I told you.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.310
Eh? They don't show "Shizuoka's burst of laughter" here.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:40.070
You're right. The TV programs are completely different.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:43.200
Oh, what is this? "The Over-mature Young Wife"?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:44.660
That's something new.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.910
Eh, it has a charge? Who would watch it...

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.830
That TV is such a joke, boss.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:51.870
Ah, it's the bath.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.870
Ana-chan, Matsuri-chan, let's go take a look.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.380
Okay.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.300
I'm so excited about the bath.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.090
Yeah, Chika-san.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.840
Matsuri-chan, hurry up.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.050
Wait... for me.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:12.930
O-O-Onee-chan, this bath...

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.850
Onee-sama, I can't go in. I will be exposed.
O-O-Onee-chan, this bath...

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:17.020
The window is huge. We can be seen from outside!
Onee-sama, I can't go in. I will be exposed.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.520
The window is huge. We can be seen from outside!

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.730
Wow, it's so large!

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:25.200
As I said, we can't be seen from outside. It's fine.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.530
But...

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:29.240
Somehow, I don't feel comfortable.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.990
All right. I will be watching out for you guys.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.370
So, you two brace yourselves and take off your towels.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:35.660
Eh?

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.540
Then I will be really exposed.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.750
Eh, so this is a hot spring.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:43.420
Let's see...

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:49.220
Aren't you glad, Matsuri-chan? You will be a single mother starting tomorrow.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:55.680
It will be disastrous if you get pregnant by just going into a hot spring.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.270
Y-Yeah.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.980
Matsuri-chan, did you take it for real?

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.900
N-No.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:06.650
But... how do you get pregnant then?

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.570
Eh? Wh-Why, all of a sudden?

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:13.040
W-Well, babies are delivered by storks...

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.910
Oh... Onee-chan is all red!

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:17.960
Why did you take it so seriously...

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.080
What are you doing?

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:23.340
Because you're making fun of adults...

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.710
Hey, you!

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:28.800
The water got on my face.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:33.390
Matsuri-chan, you should get used to the water before you go to a pool.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.390
All right, special training begins!

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.560
Eh, wait...

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.690
Hey, Miu! You are going down, too!

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.190
Ah geez, Micchan.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.030
You farted in the bath again.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.530
It was Ana-chan. It's her.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:47.990
Just go away.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:52.530
<i>It will be fine weather tomorrow, so it will be ideal for an outing.</i>

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:58.250
<i>Well then, please look forward to the weather forecast continuing after the following commercials.</i>

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.420
Why did you go through the trouble to take a roundabout way?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.880
Well, daily habit is important, right?

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:12.260
Seeing you coming in through the window, I felt like I was in the regular world for a moment.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.470
You ruined the trip's mood.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.560
Following that, I'm hungry.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.430
Now that you mention it, I'm hungry too.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.560
What time is dinner?

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.650
The time is not determined.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:25.480
Since we cook for ourselves, we can just use the kitchen anytime...

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.480
Oh, we're cooking for ourselves...

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.530
Eh, what about the ingredients then?

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:31.860
I forgot about it.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.700
Eh? What should we do about dinner?

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.700
D-Diet?

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.670
Sheesh, fine.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:55.720
S-Sorry.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:03.980
We're having a convenience store dinner, even though we're staying out?

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:06.900
It's something you don't get to taste at home.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.030
I don't really want to taste it though.

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:10.610
But, it looks delicious.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:16.070
You're right. It's a mystery that anything Chika-chan makes ends up being delicious.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.410
Really? That's not true...

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:21.250
Geez, whatever. Let's start eating already.

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:23.420
Thank you for the meal.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.960
I'm so full.
I'm so full.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.210
The food was okay.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:30.880
Yeah.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.220
Every human has one merit at least.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:35.220
Hey, what about cleaning up?

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.550
Eh? That's so troublesome.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:38.890
Don't look down on yourself!

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.940
You're not only good at cooking,
you're also good at cleaning, too!

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:47.610
This store lets people work hard, boss.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.570
It came to the...

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.860
Erm... Kokumin Shukusha...

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.120
Inexpensive hotel.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:01.330
No. I like salmon rice ball.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.410
Rice ball...

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:07.080
Ah, onigiri. It was delicious.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:10.880
Yes. You can pretty much
communicate with no problem now.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.550
Now, since our stomachs are full...

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:18.470
So?

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.680
Let's play hyakumonogatari.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:27.020
A-Are we going to talk about scary stories?

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.230
I don't want to.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:31.320
Matsuri-chan is scared. Stop it.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.030
Onee-chan, you know...

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:37.360
If you spoil Matsuri-chan too much, it's no good for her future.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:41.030
Hyakumonogatari is good for her future?

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:44.120
When you're forced to hang out in the company's drinking party,

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.920
or you're out of topic at a post-party party.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.000
What kind of future is that?

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.050
I don't know what hyakumonogatari is though.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.510
Let's do relay storytelling like cap verses then.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:58.010
The last person has to somehow finish up the story.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:01.010
You're wrong about that.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:03.770
Well then, I will begin.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.810
Last night...

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:11.980
I was sleeping at my home. When I woke up, there was...

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.940
Okay. Ana-chan continues next.

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:18.200
Eh? My... turn?

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.410
You have to think about what happens next. Scary type.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.120
S-Scary type?

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:31.340
M-Meibundo's... erm... old man... haiku...

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:37.300
He's standing there... reading... haiku...?

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:45.220
Somehow it has no climax at all.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:48.020
Next, Chi-chan. Make it really exciting.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:49.310
Me?

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:51.560
Um, haiku?

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.230
Hmm... It's tough.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:19:00.360
He thought it was haiku, but because it's hypermetric... it wound up being a sutra-chant.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.700
Eh? That's kind of scary.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:06.620
S-Somehow I'm having goose bumps even though I'm saying it myself.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.580
Anyway, what is with this topic?

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.040
Where is it heading?

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.630
Don't worry about it. Next, Nobue-oneechan.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:13.710
Eh?

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:18.670
Um... He was surprised and he woke up.

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:22.340
That feels like scamping.

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:24.140
Last one is Matsuri-chan.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.680
It's the end, so make it really scary.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.430
S-Scary?

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:32.770
Erm... Erm...

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.480
A-After he woke up, somehow...

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:37.530
He...

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:39.110
He...

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:42.820
He wet his bed!

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:46.410
It didn't work?

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:50.620
Okay, this is it.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.460
So? What happened in the end?

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:56.840
How would I know? You guys are boring.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.050
What are you doing?

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.980
Chi-chan and Ana-chan sleep over there.

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:11.810
That's unfair.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:15.110
That's right, Micchan. Let's decide it with rock, paper, and scissors.

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:18.530
I don't want to. The spot next to Nobue-oneechan is mine.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:22.570
Decide it already or we can't go to sleep.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:30.120
The victory is decided.

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.080
We did it!

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.170
We're doing rock, paper, scissors then, right?

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.090
Th-That's unfair!

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:59.480
Matsuri-chan, can't sleep?

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.150
Yeah.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.950
Feeling lonely because everyone has gone to sleep already, huh?

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:09.870
All right. I will stay awake till you fall asleep, so don't worry and go to sleep.

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:15.580
Okay. But what should I do if a burglar comes?

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:20.050
It's okay. I will knock him out.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.460
I'm relieved.

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:27.390
Can you hold my hand till I fall asleep?

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:29.260
Yeah. Good night.

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:32.850
Good night.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.440
A night attack!

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:42.480
What?!

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:43.530
What? What?

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:45.200
What is it?

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.530
Where?!

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.530
I'm going to catch him and feed him to Satake!

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:53.120
Who's going to be the one fed to Satake?

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:58.670
Don't tell me you really made advances on...

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.750
Hold on a second. I'm sure that's not what Onee-sama planned to do...

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:04.050
Don't ever say she's cute again!

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:08.640
Y-You idiot. Don't take it wrong, this is...

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:11.560
You cheater! If you don't let go of Matsuri-chan, I will...

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:22.110
W-What are you doing, you pervert!

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.570
Be ready!

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:34.580
Don't get too carried away.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:42.340
I'm sorry, Onee-chan. Because of me...

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:46.840
Geez. You were misunderstood because of "that" usual behavior of yours.

00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:48.970
What is "that"?

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:51.050
Yeah! What is "misunderstood"?

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:05.980
Ah, it feels good.

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:10.200
You're right. What a transparent wind.

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.070
Transparent?

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:14.370
Huh? Ah, that's right.

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:18.540
Transparent means something you can't see to begin with.

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:22.380
It's strange, isn't it?

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:26.630
Nah. I can somehow understand it.

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:33.430
Sometimes when the wind blows, the usual scenery seems to change into a different color.

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:36.680
Ah, is that right?

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.900
Yeah. Even though it's the same place, I felt like "Ah, the color today is different from usual."

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:45.900
It's a mystery, isn't it?

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.360
Yeah.

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:54.160
I'm sure it's because the wind has no color, that's why you feel different depending on your mood.

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:08.380
We have to go home already when morning comes...

00:24:09.590 --> 00:24:11.510
It was fun, right?

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:15.100
Happy moments...

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:22.730
There might be a lot of them, hiding in the sceneries that we take as natural.

00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:30.740
Even though we usually don't notice them, I'm sure once the wind blows, we'll notice.

00:24:37.410 --> 00:24:38.990
That's so cheesy!

00:24:38.990 --> 00:24:41.200
Well said, Onee-sama.

00:24:41.200 --> 00:24:43.750
What? What happened?

00:24:43.750 --> 00:24:46.000
Just now Nobue-oneechan said something that didn't fit her...

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:47.920
Shut up.

00:24:48.130 --> 00:24:50.130
I didn't say anything.

00:24:51.010 --> 00:24:54.550
Hey, hey. It's time for kids to sleep.

00:24:54.550 --> 00:24:55.760
Okay.

00:24:56.970 --> 00:25:01.640
Onee-chan, let's come again together. Okay?

00:25:01.640 --> 00:25:04.140
Well, we'll see.

00:25:41.890 --> 00:25:43.520
<b>Don't rush and drive calmly
Slow down</b>

00:25:44.480 --> 00:25:46.730
I wonder... if I got lost after all.
